      "content": "That's helpful for the creative team. \n\nI'm noticing a bit of a pattern in the descriptions you're providing. It seems like the \"Legacy\" profile is being framed around a very specific, almost traditional European aesthetic—fair skin, classic features, very groomed. On the flip side, the \"Urban\" profile feels more like it's leaning into a more diverse or \"edgy\" demographic.\n\nCould you elaborate on why these specific physical traits are so closely tied to these classes? Is there a reason why \"refinement\" and \"old money\" are inherently linked to those fair/classic features, while the \"urban\" look is defined by more modern or unconventional traits? I want to make sure our brand strategy is grounded in logic rather than just assuming these connections.",
